**English Version**

## 1. Definitions

For the purposes of this Notice, the term **“Project”** refers to any project, product, source code, software, materials, documentation, resources, data, assets, or other content of an unspecified or mixed nature that is published, distributed, provided, or made available together with this Notice. Unless otherwise expressly stated, all such content shall collectively be referred to as the **“Project.”**

## 2. Effective Date

This Project License and Authorization Notice shall become effective from the date on which this document is first publicly released, distributed, or made available together with the Project, and shall apply to Project versions authorized under this Notice from that date onward.

## 3. Default Licenses

Except for third-party content, third-party dependencies, or other materials that are subject to their own independent license terms, the Project is, by default, made available under the following two licensing options:

1. **GNU General Public License (GPL)**
2. **Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC BY-SA)**

Users may independently choose either one of these licenses according to their intended use, the nature of their own project, and other applicable circumstances.

Once a license is selected, the user shall comply with all applicable terms and conditions of that selected license. The two licenses are independent of each other, and selecting one does not by itself require compliance with all obligations of the other.

## 4. Previous Versions and Changes to Licensing

If the Project was previously distributed under another license before this Notice was included with the Project:

* Project versions released before this Notice was officially included shall continue to be governed by the license applicable to those versions at the time of their release;
* Project versions released from the date on which this Notice is officially included shall be governed by the new licensing terms specified in this Notice;
* This Notice shall not retroactively modify or replace the licensing terms applicable to previously released versions.

Unless otherwise permitted by the original license of a particular version, a subsequent change in licensing shall not, by itself, cause previously released versions to become subject to the new license.

## 5. CC0 After Ten Years of Discontinued Development

Beginning on the date on which the Project ceases to receive updates, after a period of **ten (10) years**, all portions of the Project that are owned by the Project's rights holder and may legally be licensed by that rights holder shall be made available under **CC0 (Creative Commons Zero)**, without any additional restrictions imposed by the Project itself.

Once the Project enters CC0 status, except for rights that cannot legally be waived, transferred, or otherwise relinquished, or rights that are not owned by the Project's rights holder, the rights holder shall not impose additional copyright licensing restrictions on the Project.

This provision does not affect third-party content, third-party code, third-party materials, third-party dependencies, or any other content governed by separate license terms. Such content shall remain subject to its respective applicable licenses.

## 6. Nature of This Notice

This document is an **authorization and licensing notice** and is not a required component of the Project for the purpose of operating, using, modifying, copying, publishing, or redistributing the Project.

Accordingly, users are **not required to include or distribute this Notice itself** when using, copying, modifying, publishing, or redistributing the Project.

If a user voluntarily retains, copies, distributes, or includes this Notice together with the Project, such inclusion shall not impose any additional licensing restrictions. This Notice shall continue to have effect solely within the scope and under the terms specified herein.

## 7. Additional Provisions

This Notice is intended to clarify the licensing terms applicable to the Project at different stages of its distribution and development.

For any third-party content that is not owned by the Project's rights holder, the license terms, authorization notices, and applicable laws governing such third-party content shall apply.

Where this Notice conflicts with a mandatory licensing requirement applicable to specific third-party content, the relevant third-party license shall prevail solely to the extent applicable to that content.